{% doc %}
  Single source of truth for Prince Tires service prices.

  Prices were typed into the copy in a lot of places — the flat-repair price
  alone appears in nine files — so changing one meant finding every copy and
  missing some. This reads them from the `service_prices` metaobject (Shopify
  admin > Content > Metaobjects > Service prices), the same pattern pt-nap uses
  for hours, so a price changes in ONE place and every consumer follows.

  Every field falls back to the value that was live when this snippet was
  written, so a missing metaobject or a missing field never renders a blank
  price on a customer-facing page.

  @param {string} field - Which price to output. One of:
      install_per_tire | install_own_per_tire | flat_repair | balancing_per_wheel | balancing_set |
      rotation | rotation_hd | rotation_per_tire | rotation_truck_per_tire | changeover |
      changeover_per_tire | changeover_truck_per_tire | changeover_trailer |
      winter_from | winter_premium_from | winter_premium_to

  The seasonal swap is priced PER TIRE since 2026-11-02 (the app's db/088):
  changeover_per_tire ($15 car / SUV / van / EV / dually) and
  changeover_truck_per_tire ($20 truck / large truck); a trailer stays
  changeover_trailer ($100 flat). `changeover` keeps its meaning — a car's set
  of four ($60) — for copy that quotes the usual job. The three new fields are
  not on the metaobject yet, so they render their fallbacks until an admin adds
  them there; the booking forms price from the app's catalogue either way.

  @example
  {% render 'pt-prices', field: 'flat_repair' %}            {# "$50" #}
  {%- capture p %}{% render 'pt-prices', field: 'rotation' %}{% endcapture -%}
  Rotation is priced PER TIRE since 2026-11-13: rotation_per_tire ($15 car /
  SUV / van / EV) and rotation_truck_per_tire ($20 pickup / heavy truck /
  dually), always the whole set. `rotation` stays a car's set of four ($60);
  `rotation_hd` is no longer quoted anywhere.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign sp = metaobjects['service_prices']['current']

  case field
    when 'install_per_tire'     
      assign fallback = '$30'
    when 'install_own_per_tire'
      assign fallback = '$30'
    when 'install_own_per_tire'
      assign fallback = '$30'
    when 'flat_repair'          
      assign fallback = '$50'
    when 'balancing_per_wheel'  
      assign fallback = '$20'
    when 'balancing_set'        
      assign fallback = '$80'
    when 'rotation'             
      assign fallback = '$60'
    when 'rotation_hd'          
      assign fallback = '$100'
    when 'rotation_per_tire'
      assign fallback = '$15'
    when 'rotation_truck_per_tire'
      assign fallback = '$20'
    when 'changeover'           
      assign fallback = '$60'
    when 'changeover_per_tire'
      assign fallback = '$15'
    when 'changeover_truck_per_tire'
      assign fallback = '$20'
    when 'changeover_trailer'
      assign fallback = '$100'
    when 'winter_from'          
      assign fallback = '$130'
    when 'winter_premium_from'  
      assign fallback = '$240'
    when 'winter_premium_to'    
      assign fallback = '$380'
    else
      assign fallback = ''
  endcase

  assign value = ''
  if sp != blank
    assign value = sp[field].value | default: '' | strip
  endif
  if value == blank
    assign value = fallback
  endif

  echo value
-%}
